From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:10:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): prove key absence across moving Board snapshots
 [daveey]

A busy Board cannot hold one global head across all task pages. Cover the finite first-to-last page interval with contiguous authenticated full-row changes instead; reject every key match and all incomplete, failed, compacted or gapped feeds. Preserve the original 30-second bound, identity/absence gates and byte-retaining receipts. This is observational absence at the final cut, not a key reservation. No service deployment or production repair.

Proof: original constant-head veto fails busy-board regression; 206 tests pass across all seven reserved-key consumers, scripts/check passes all 21 checks. Includes insert behind cursor, update, transient duplicate, malformed/missing/compacted feed, finite cut while writers advance and stale evidence. Operational repair remains t_22adfd77b74f44c1.
